==Overview==
<tabber>
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Very high combo potential.
** Good for any playstyle due to having stuns.
* Good for farming since both moves have [[AoE]] and no knockback.
* Moves are extremely fast.
* Low mastery requirements.

|'''[Z] Soul Beam'''
* Can [[Instinct Break|break Instinct]].
* Stuns for a long time.
* High speed.

|'''[X] Soul Slashes'''
* Good combo extender.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* [[Blade]] users are immune.
* Requires a lot of skill to utilize its full potential.
* Required RNG to obtained, since you need to wait [[Island Secrets]] to be triggered on Magma Village.
* Low damage compared to other swords.
* Small hitbox.
* Short range.

|'''[Z] Soul Beam'''
* Hard to hit.
* Can only break [[Instinct]] if it's a headshot.

|'''[X] Soul Slashes'''
* Can be [[Instinct]]-tricked.
* Long attack.
* Locks the user in place, making them vulnerable.
}}
</tabber>

==Trivia==
* Despite being one of the earliest swords added in-game, the Soul Cane is still good for [[PvP mechanics|PvP]].
* The Soul Cane is the second most expensive sword in the [[First Sea]], the first being [[Bisento]].
* The way Soul Cane is held is known as the "reverse grip" (in real life combat), which is often not practiced due to the technique lacking range, protection and power in ranged combat. 
** The Soul Cane is held the exact same way as the [[Gravity Blade]].

